@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy notice";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">
    <strong>Draft notice:</strong>
    </div>

<h2>1. Who operates this service</h2>
<p>
    This service is operated by <strong>[name of the organisation]</strong>, at
    <strong>[postal address]</strong>. We can be contacted at
    <strong>[privacy contact email or other contact details]</strong>.
</p>

<h2>2. Information this service uses</h2>
<p>When you use the service, it processes:</p>
<ul>
    <li>The NHS number, surname, and date of birth you enter.</li>
    <li>The NHS number, name, and date of birth returned by the patient lookup service.</li>
    <li>Your answers to three questions about drinking, smoking, and exercise.</li>
    <li>Information calculated from those details and answers, including your verified age, score, and low or high result category.</li>
    <li>A session identifier stored in a necessary browser cookie, and temporary session values used to keep your place in the service.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The application uses these details to check the patient record, check the minimum age requirement,
    calculate a result, and move you through the pages. It does not ask for your address, phone number,
    email address, or appointment information.
</p>

<h2>3. Patient record lookup</h2>
<p>
    The service sends the NHS number you enter to the patient lookup API at
    <code>https://al-tech-test-apim.azure-api.net/tech-test/t2/patients/{nhsNumber}</code>.
    The API returns a patient record containing an NHS number, name, and date of birth. The application
    compares those returned details with the surname and date of birth you entered. It does not send
    your entered surname or date of birth to this API.
</p>
<p>
    The API is operated by <strong>[Organisation]</strong>
</p>

<h2>4. Lifestyle answers and result</h2>
<p>
    The service uses your age and answers to the questions about drinking, smoking, and exercise to
    calculate a score and show a low or high result. A score of 3 or less produces the low result; a
    score of 4 or more produces the high result. This result is generated automatically by the application.
</p>
<p>
    The application code processes your submitted answers to calculate the score, but does not save the
    answers in its session, a database, or a file. It temporarily stores the result category in the session
    so it can display the result page.
</p>

<h2>5. Legal basis</h2>
<p>
    <strong>[Legal basis]
    </strong>
</p>

<h2>6. Who receives the information</h2>
<p>
    The NHS number is sent to the patient lookup API described above. The service is also hosted by
    <strong>[Host]</strong>.
</p>

<h2>7. How long information is kept</h2>
<p>
    The application keeps temporary session information in server memory. This includes the pass flag
    and verified age while you answer the questions, followed by the result category while the result page
    is available. The application clears the flow values as you start again or complete the questionnaire.
    Session information is also subject to the configured session expiry and may be lost when the
    application restarts. The application code does not save patient details or answers to a database or
    file.
</p>

<h2>8. Cookies</h2>
<p>
    The service uses an ASP.NET Core session cookie to maintain your session. Its forms also use
    anti-forgery protection. These cookies support the service and its security.
</p>

<h2>9. Your rights and how to contact us</h2>
<p>
    Depending on the lawful basis and circumstances, you may have rights to request access to, correction
    of, deletion of, or limits on the use of your personal information, and to object to some uses. To ask
    a question or make a request, contact <strong>[privacy contact details]</strong>.
</p>
<p>
    You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">ico.org.uk</a>.
</p>

<h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
<p>
    We will update this notice if the service or its use of personal information changes. The current
    version will be available from the service's Privacy page.
</p>
